  "extraction_notes": "Amazon 2025 Sustainability Report, data-centre water section. Amazon DOES use the WRI Aqueduct Water Risk Atlas (2030 business-as-usual baseline scenario) and reports the share of data-centre withdrawal by water-stress level (48% low, 22% high/extremely high in 2025). Also captures 2025 data-centre withdrawal (9.4 bn L), withdrawal-based WUE (0.15 in 2024, 0.12 in 2025), water-positive progress (53% 2024 -> 75% 2025), replenishment returned (9.4 bn L in 2025; >18 bn L contracted), and avoided/preserved water (938 M L cooling reduced; 849 M L potable preserved). Withdrawal only: no consumption or discharge split, so SWI-C is not derivable from AWS. Not workload- or region-attributed; not Azure/GCP-equivalent service factor."
}